WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:07.916
In this video you’ll put a picture of your site under your map.

2
00:00:07.916 --> 00:00:11.368
It can be a hand sketch, a site plan, or an aerial photo.

3
00:00:11.368 --> 00:00:12.943
Then you’ll trace over it.

4
00:00:13.395 --> 00:00:18.930
Start a new map at your site. This time pick Start blank, then Create blank map.

5
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.147
Open the Layers tab and choose Upload site plan or aerial photo.

6
00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:27.981
A phone photo of a paper sketch works fine.

7
00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:33.418
The picture goes on its own layer and is locked, so it won’t move while you draw.

8
00:00:33.418 --> 00:00:35.141
Choose Fit to see all of it.

9
00:00:35.593 --> 00:00:41.461
If the picture is hard to draw over, make it lighter with the Opacity slider.

10
00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:45.344
Now go back to Add and choose Draw a row of spaces.

11
00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:48.371
Drag along the front of a row in your sketch.

12
00:00:48.371 --> 00:00:50.726
The app counts how many spaces fit.

13
00:00:51.177 --> 00:00:56.724
Check the number of spaces. Then type the row letter in Prefix, and choose Create.

14
00:00:57.587 --> 00:00:59.506
Do the same for the next row.

15
00:00:59.506 --> 00:01:04.004
Drag along the front of the row, type its letter, and choose Create.

16
00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:11.657
Rows can also be at an angle. Drag along the angled row, and the row turns to match.

17
00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:19.984
For a curved lane, search the library for curved, and add a curved driving lane.

18
00:01:20.435 --> 00:01:24.655
Now drag each end of the curved lane to the ends of the lane in your sketch.

19
00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:26.654
You can move them again at any time.

20
00:01:29.303 --> 00:01:33.705
Then drag the two bend handles until the curve follows the lane in your sketch.

21
00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:35.265
The map updates as you drag.

22
00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:41.903
When you’re done, hide the picture from the Layers tab to see your map on its own.

23
00:01:41.903 --> 00:01:43.693
Everything you traced stays.
